Package: selectools
Type: Package
Title: A facilitating model selection procedure
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person(
      c("Lucas", "D."), "Lalande",
      email = "lalande.luke@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c("0000-0001-9319-8033")
    )
Description: The goal of 'selectools' is to provide and facilitate model selection procedures, 
    mostly based on AIC and AICc, and adapting the 'dredge' function from the 'MuMIn' 
    package. 'selectools' contains a set of function to perform trajectory analyses.
    It is designed for model selection from A to Z when testing different 
    trajectories as can be done in senescence research, by automatically computing, fitting, 
    testing, comparing and ranking constant, linear, quadratic, factor and threshold trajectories. 
    The package also includes a function ('pglmm_dredge') to perform model 
    selection of phylogenetic generalized linear mixed models ('pglmm' from the 'phyr' package). 
    It generates a model selection table of models as would do the 'dredge' function 
    from 'MuMIn' with combinations (subsets) of fixed effect terms in the global model, 
    with optional model inclusion rules.
